`unset` on `LINENO`, a parameter the shell owns, leaves its export letter, so
the value assigned next reaches a child; a name the script made loses it.
Measured 2026-10-03 on dash 0.5.12 under `env -i`. See
Semantics.UnsetKeepsTheShellsOwnAttributes.

-- script the-shells-own --
export LINENO=5; unset LINENO; LINENO=7
/usr/bin/env | while read -r kv; do case $kv in LINENO=*|FOO=*) echo "$kv";; esac; done
-- out --
LINENO=7
-- script the-scripts-own --
export FOO=1; unset FOO; FOO=2
/usr/bin/env | while read -r kv; do case $kv in LINENO=*|FOO=*) echo "$kv";; esac; done
-- out noeol --
